chmod (change mode) is used to change access permissions of files in directory

Categories (- means file, d means directory, l means link)
Symbolic syntax (who)(operation)(permission)
(u,g,o,a)(+, -, =)(r,w,x)

Numeric syntax
Read 4
Write 2
Execute 1

-R (change permission for a folder and everything inside it)
eg. chmod -R u+w,go-w project-directory/

This adds write permission for owner and removes write permission for other and groups in all files and directories recursively

Common Perm. Sets
Permission  Numeric    Use case
rwxr-xr-x   755             Direc.,scripts
rw-r--r--   644               Regular&config files
rwx------   700               Priv./sensitive script

Audit file means checking who has access to what

To make a file executable i.e able to run
chmod +x filename
(to run the file and output, use echo before your content, echo means print) to test ./filename

chown (owner:group)
to change ownership
* sudo command is required because changing owners require administrative privileges
eg. sudo chown john:developer file.txt 
sudo chown john:john /home/documents (directories)
